+    // device/vivo/1907N: removed - these AIDL vintf_fragments collide at the exact same
+    // install path (vendor/etc/vintf/manifest/android.hardware.wifi.{supplicant,hostapd}.xml)
+    // as our real device's own genuinely-HIDL vivo stock blobs (vendor/vivo/1907N/Android.bp's
+    // prebuilt_etc_xml modules of the same names, sourced from real stock firmware extraction).
+    // This apex is Cuttlefish's own virtual-device WiFi implementation and is otherwise
+    // irrelevant to a real device, but Soong's own directory scanning builds and installs it
+    // regardless of product config (confirmed: no PRODUCT_PACKAGES reference pulls it in, and
+    // excluding it via PRODUCT_PACKAGES := $(filter-out ...) had no effect either) -
+    // BUILD_BROKEN_DUP_RULES was silently letting this wrong AIDL declaration win the
+    // collision, which broke Wi-Fi entirely (SupplicantStaIfaceHal/HostapdHal's own
+    // serviceDeclared() trusts the VINTF manifest and never fell back to the real HIDL service
+    // that's genuinely there). prebuilt_etc_xml (what our real fragments use) doesn't support
+    // Soong's overrides: property, so removing the fragments here - the actual root of the
+    // collision - was the only way to resolve this deterministically rather than relying on
+    // BUILD_BROKEN_DUP_RULES' arbitrary winner-picking. See device git history.
+    // vintf_fragments: [
+    //     ":android.hardware.wifi.supplicant.xml",
